==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|morn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|morgen}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*morgan}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*morgin}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*murginaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*mr̥kéno}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mr̥kóno}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*mr̥Hko}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*mer-|t=to shimmer, glisten}}.

See also {{cog|fy|moarn}}, {{cog|nds|Morgen}}, {{cog|nl|morgen}}, {{cog|de|Morgen}}, {{cog|da|morgen}}, {{cog|no|morgon}}; also  <!--{{cog|cy|bore|t=morning}}, -->{{cog|lt|mérkti|t=to blink, twinkle}}, {{cog|sa|मरीचि|tr=márīci|t=ray of light}}, {{cog|el|μέρα|t=morning}}. {{doublet|en|morrow|morgen}}. See also {{m|en|morning}}.

